{"id":"9180b65c-c09e-408c-b432-067930389475","object":"chat.completion","created":1785031643,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case.get(\\\"threshold\\\")\\n    if threshold is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing threshold\\\")\\n    calls = case.get(\\\"calls\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing or invalid calls\\\")\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call.get(\\\"call_id\\\")\\n        if call_id is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Missing call_id in call\\\")\\n        loss_without = call.get(\\\"loss_without_call\\\")\\n        loss_with = call.get(\\\"loss_with_call\\\")\\n        pred_tokens = call.get(\\\"prediction_tokens\\\")\\n        parseable = call.get(\\\"parseable\\\")\\n        if any(v is None for v in [loss_without, loss_with, pred_tokens, parseable]):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required fields in call\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the task: implement solve(case) for AGENT-TF-01. The goal is to filter API calls based on gain normalized by at least one prediction token, requiring parseable and normalized gain >= threshold. Return accepted_call_ids list and diagnostics list with per-call details.\n\nThe output schema is given: accepted_call_ids (array of strings), diagnostics (array of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain). Must not add extra properties.\n\nFrom the payload: threshold is a number, calls is array of objects each with call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable.\n\nFor each call:\n- compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n- normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (since \"normalize gain by at least one prediction token\"? Actually \"normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" means divide by prediction_tokens? Or maybe it's gain per token? The phrase: \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" Could mean divide by number of prediction tokens. Usually normalized gain = gain / prediction_tokens. But \"at least one\" might hint that if prediction_tokens is 0, but it's always >0 in examples? However, we should handle zero? But the field is \"prediction_tokens\" and examples have positive numbers. For safety, we can assume >0. But the task says \"validate every required field\". If prediction_tokens is zero, would cause error? Possibly treat as invalid? But we'll assume positive. The condition: \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" So accepted if parseable == True and normalized_gain >= threshold.\n\nThen round normalized_gain? The output says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" and normalized_gain type is number. Probably need to round to some precision? Not specified. The examples: maybe no rounding needed? But we can keep as float or round to maybe 8 decimals? Since no specific rounding, we'll just compute and return as float (JSON number). The \"rounded\" might just mean compute correctly. We'll keep as computed value.\n\nOrder: diagnostics in supplied call order. So iterate over case[\"calls\"] in order, compute for each, return diagnostics in that order.\n\naccepted_call_ids: list of call_ids where accepted is True.\n\nReturn dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nEdge cases: if threshold negative? Then all parseable accepted. Not needed.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) function that takes dict payload.\n\nImplementation must be Python source code as JSON string in the response under \"implementation\" key.\n\nWe'll produce Python code.\n\nPotential pitfalls: must not mutate case; use only standard library; raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. For example, if threshold is missing or calls is not list, etc. But the schema ensures it. We'll include validation: check \"threshold\" present, \"calls\" present and list, each call has required fields. If any missing, raise ValueError.\n\nAlso ensure no additional keys in output.\n\nImplement rounding? Not specified. I'll leave as float.\n\nNow produce the JSON response with single key \"implementation\" and value as Python source string.\n\nWe need to escape the string properly for JSON.\n\nWrite code: \n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case.get(\"threshold\")\n    if threshold is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing threshold\")\n    calls = case.get(\"calls\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing or invalid calls\")\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call.get(\"call_id\")\n        if call_id is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing call_id in call\")\n        loss_without = call.get(\"loss_without_call\")\n        loss_with = call.get(\"loss_with_call\")\n        pred_tokens = call.get(\"prediction_tokens\")\n        parseable = call.get(\"parseable\")\n        if any(v is None for v in [loss_without, loss_with, pred_tokens, parseable]):\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing required fields in call\")\n        # Compute\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens  # assume prediction_tokens > 0\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat's it. Note: parseable is boolean in JSON, but may be True/False. Use bool() to convert.\n\nNow return as JSON.\n\nWe'll enclose the implementation key with the Python code string escaped.\n\nLet's produce the final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1374,"total_tokens":3538,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1025},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}